inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWANAKA, TAKAHUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOMOTO, HIROHUMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TSUKADA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A fiber-reinforced rubber composition which is crosslinkable with an organic peroxide and is prepared by compounding a rubber composition prepared beforehand by mixing 75 parts of a hydrogenated NBR (iodine value, 11; acrylonitrile content, 36 %; Mooney viscosity, 120) with 15 parts of methacrylic acid and 10 parts of zinc oxide with 75 parts of a short-fiber master batch prepared by mixing 25 parts of a hydrogenated NBR (iodine value: 30 or lower) with 25 parts of polyethylene and 25 parts of short nylon fibers. The compounding of the rubber composition prepared beforehand with the short-fiber master batch is accomplished by kneading them at a temperature which is not lower than the melting point of the polyethylene and is lower than the melting point of the nylon and at a shear rate of 100 to 1,000 sec&lt;-1&gt;.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition de caoutchouc renforcée par des fibres, réticulable au moyen de peroxyde organique, et préparée par mélangeage d'une composition de caoutchouc obtenue auparavant par mélange de 75 parts de NBR hydrogéné (indice d'iode 11, contenu en acrylonitrile 36 %, viscosité Mooney 120) avec 15 parts d'un mélange monté à fibres courtes préparé par mélange de 25 parts de NBR hydrogéné (indice d'iode 30 ou moins) avec 25 parts de polyéthylène et 25 parts de fibres courtes de nylon. Le mélangeage de la composition de caoutchouc avec le mélange monté à fibres courtes est effectué par malaxage à une température qui est égale ou supérieure à celle du point de fusion du polyéthylène et qui est inférieure à celle du point de fusion du nylon, et à une vitesse de cisaillement comprise entre 100 et 1000 sec&lt;-1&gt;.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>